## Key Components

#### A web app is built using three core web technologies, and students can now use AI tools to assist in their development process.


<img src="https://images.code.org/5a14dc8bdef7c9c9b5c4d8736c451265-image-1759348130243.png" alt="HTML – the structure of a webpage (like the frame of a house).CSS – the style and design (colors, fonts, layout—how the house looks).JavaScript – the interactivity and logic (how the house “works,” like doors opening or lights turning on). AI – a creative assistant that helps suggest, refine, and debug code, while students stay in control of decisions." width="850px" style="display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;">


#### *Note: Unit One only covers HTML and CSS. JavaScript will be introduced in Unit 2*. 



## Why it matters for students:

#### **Building web apps helps students:**
- #### See the connection between code and creativity.
- #### Practice problem-solving and computational thinking.
- #### Understand how many of the tools they use every day (from Google Docs to ChatGPT) are built with the same foundational technologies.


## Next Up

#### Let's take a look at the final project the students will create in this unit. 


